From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fabricio Akio <fabricioakio@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 15:53:30 -0300
Subject: power: supply: pmi8998_fg: wait for the charger named in
 power-supplies

devm_power_supply_get_by_reference() returns NULL when the supply named
in power-supplies is not registered yet, and the probe then carries on
without the charger: no notifier is registered, so the battery supply
neither reports the charger's status nor follows its changes.
fw_devlink orders the two from power-supplies, but drops that order at
the deferred probe timeout if the charger's driver has not been loaded
by then.

Defer the probe until the named charger is registered, and look it up
before registering the battery, so that a retry does not register and
remove the battery supply each time.

Signed-off-by: Fabricio Akio <fabricioakio@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/pmi8998_fg.c | 21 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/pmi8998_fg.c b/drivers/power/supply/pmi8998_fg.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/pmi8998_fg.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/pmi8998_fg.c
@@ -625,6 +625,18 @@ static int pmi8998_fg_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		return ret;
 	}
 
+	/* The charger named in power-supplies, if any, for status checking */
+	chip->chg_psy = devm_power_supply_get_by_reference(chip->dev,
+							   "power-supplies");
+	if (!chip->chg_psy)
+		return dev_err_probe(chip->dev, -EPROBE_DEFER,
+				     "Charger supply not registered yet\n");
+	if (IS_ERR(chip->chg_psy)) {
+		ret = PTR_ERR(chip->chg_psy);
+		dev_warn(chip->dev, "Failed to get charger supply: %d\n", ret);
+		chip->chg_psy = NULL;
+	}
+
 	supply_config.drv_data = chip;
 
 	chip->batt_psy = devm_power_supply_register(chip->dev,
@@ -653,15 +665,6 @@ static int pmi8998_fg_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		return ret;
 	}
 
-	/* Optional: Get charger power supply for status checking */
-	chip->chg_psy = devm_power_supply_get_by_reference(chip->dev,
-							   "power-supplies");
-	if (IS_ERR(chip->chg_psy)) {
-		ret = PTR_ERR(chip->chg_psy);
-		dev_warn(chip->dev, "Failed to get charger supply: %d\n", ret);
-		chip->chg_psy = NULL;
-	}
-
 	if (chip->chg_psy) {
 		INIT_DELAYED_WORK(&chip->status_changed_work,
 				  pmi8998_fg_status_changed_worker);
-- 
